### applying the "hwe-0.05" filter
I am doing this combined for all the species

vcftools \
--vcf filtered_mac3.recode.vcf \
--hwe 0.05 \
--recode \
--out filtered_mac3_hwe

// filtered_mac3_hwe.recode.vcf - this vcf file will be created

## What this does ##
--hwe 0.05
removes SNPs with: HWE p-value < 0.05
These are variants that significantly deviate from Hardy–Weinberg expectations.
Biological meaning
Variants failing HWE may indicate: sequencing/genotyping errors, paralogous mapping, contamination, strong selection,population structure/inbreeding
So filtering helps improve SNP reliability.

